# Persistence and boundaries

- **GitHub-first:** `apps/api` is a thin GitHub gateway (OAuth/App, repo read/write). Do not build product features that require the Node server to manage the user’s disk.
- **Dev-local only:** Sibling/`zmk-config` layout+keymap HTTP routes are a **development adapter**. Prefer implementing file behavior in `packages/keymap-core` so GitHub (and later browser FS/clipboard) share one contract.
- **Host layouts in the browser:** User layouts and the legend view persist in IndexedDB (v3). Do not add API routes that read or write host maps. Loading layouts from a keyboard repo (`host_keymap/`) is future work and needs an ADR.
- **No concrete keyboards in domain logic:** `keymap-core` and `apps/web` product sources outside tests and the Demo loader (`apps/web/src/lib/demo/`) must not name a board in compose, host-layout registry, or other domain code. LARK host files are fixtures under `packages/keymap-core/fixtures/lark/`; other Demo boards live under `fixtures/demo/` and are listed in that catalog.
- **Domain in core:** ZMK parse/generate, DTS import/splice, the host-layout registry, compose, and **keycap legends** (`L1`, `⌃`, compact chords, hold-tap, host glyphs) belong in `packages/keymap-core`, not only in Svelte components or ad-hoc API helpers.
- **Vision / ADRs:** Before changing persistence or package roles, read `docs/TARGET_SYSTEM.md`, [ADR 0001](../../docs/adr/0001-persistence-github-first.md), and [ADR 0002](../../docs/adr/0002-keymap-file-contract.md) (save paths / JSON / `#define`).
- **Round-trip care:** Do not silently replace a custom `.keymap` with the default “THIS FILE WAS GENERATED” template when an existing file or `.keymap.template` can be used. Follow ADR 0002 (`buildKeymapCode` order).
